Nesting of member functions occurs when a member function of a class calls another member function of the same class directly without using the dot operator on an object.

Example:
class Number {
    int n;
public:
    int square() { return n * n; }
    void display() {
        cout << "Square is " << square(); // Nested call
    }
};

